Y1. C#1 (Smooth representative in a specified class of Cl(-4kN)):
- Toy audit [MEASURED / KNOWN]: C's toy (toy.py:31-75) does not test wide-box decoding of a given class. First, it picks prime leading coefficients A in [0.55, 0.75] sqrt(kN) first and solves b^2 = -kN (mod A) (toy.py:49-54), which is SIQS/MPQS form generation, not solving a specified target class. Second, its 476 vs 70 (6.8x at 16b) and 17 vs 5 (3.4x at 24b) gain comes purely from Knuth-Schroeppel multiplier scoring sum_{l<=97} (-kN/l) log(l)/l. Testing L_d[a] multipliers can bias at most the first ~ (log d)^a primes; by Mertens' theorem, sum_{p <= (log d)^a} log(p)/p = O(log log d), shifting effective log-norm by O(log log d) and changing Dickman rho(u) by L_d[o(1)] (constant/sub-L only, zero exponent gain).
- Wide-box pricing via 2D discriminant invariance + C's GRH bound + Theorem SS [PROVED in lattice/sampling models]: For ANY subexponential box side E = L_d[beta] (0 < beta < 1), log(sqrt(d) E^2) = (1/2 + o(1)) log d, so smooth norm density is rho((1/2 log d)/log B) = L_d[1 - a]^{-1} at B = L_d[a]; existence forces beta >= 1 - a. In that wide box, EVERY single-modulus root sublattice Lambda_P = {(x, y) : x = r y (mod P)} (P <= E^2, Gauss-reduced basis e_1, e_2 of det P) yields an integral cofactor form Q_tilde(u, v) = Q(u e_1 + v e_2) / P of the EXACT SAME discriminant disc(Q_tilde) = disc(Q) = -4kN, representing [Q][a_P]^{-1} in Cl(D) [PROVED, verified]. Applying C's own GRH small-box bound (harvest.md:15-19) to [Q][a_P]^{-1} proves Q_tilde(u, v) has no B-smooth value for |u|, |v| <= L_d[a] outside a 1/L_d[1 - a, Omega(1)] fraction of classes, so any slope/Johnson-radius lattice call (such as subthird's M2 slope decoder) needs >= L_d[1 - a] moduli P (total cost >= L_d[max(a, 1 - a)] >= L_d[1/2]). Scanning larger (u, v) in Lambda_P IS a plain class-group lattice sieve, priced by Theorem SS (suffmap_results.md:157-196) at >= L_d[1 - a] per witness (again >= L_d[1/2]).
- What survives: Only a non-lattice, beyond-Johnson 2D CRT one-witness list-decoder (subthird_results.md:76-79, crtdecode in 2D) intersecting prime-root congruences up to full norm P_full ~ sqrt(d) E^2 >> E^2 without stepping through index-P sublattices. P(a < 1/3) <= 0.1%.

Y2. C#2 (One 2-isogeny neighbour mod N from j alone):
- Verdict [PROVED]: C's Legendre-parameter masked-fibre reduction (4/9 split against any deterministic root selector on the doubly-split locus; harvest.md:23-25, toy.py:140-163) is a clean sharpening of conn_cmp.md:121, removing the random-root assumption. However, as an algorithmic target, finding one root of the modular cubic Phi_2(j, X) = 0 (mod N) from j alone IS depressed-cubic root extraction mod N with no extra exploitable structure.
- Why no easy regime applies: By Cardano over Z[1/6], solving Phi_2(j, X) = 0 (mod N) reduces to one square root mod N (Rabin) and one cube root in (Z/N)[sqrt(Delta)] (RSA/cubic residuosity). Pure ring trees on j cannot isolate one of the three symmetric roots without splitting N (factorbits_results.md:303-358, Theorem PT). Frobenius/Cantor-Zassenhaus powering fails because for h_i in F_p, h_i^N = (h_i^p)^q = h_i^q != h_i (mod p) (nonsmooth_results.md:313-357, Prop FROB; prim_results.md:154-158). Volcano walks require solving Phi_2 at step 1, Kani/SIDH requires torsion images not present in scalar j, and uniform lambda mod N hits tiny-CM j with negligible probability O(N^{-1/2}). Killed as a sub-1/3 route (P < 0.05%).

Y3. G#1 (CRT-HNP multi-sample biased-residue lattice):
- Lattice novelty [KNOWN in disguise]: Not new. Look at the target vector v_q = (qW, q s_{1,p}, ..., q s_{m,p}) in L_W: s_{i,q} never enters v_q! Smallness mod ONE prime factor p suffices (as long as x_i != s_{i,p} over Z). With x_0 = N = q p (exact) and x_i = k_i p + s_{i,p} (|s_{i,p}| <= N^sigma), L_W is the classical primal simultaneous-Diophantine dual of multi-sample Approximate Common Divisor (ACD) with one exact multiple (Lagarias 1982; Howgrave-Graham CaLC 2001; Cohn-Heninger 2013; dual to May-Ritzenhofen 2009 implicit factoring).
- Information conservation [PROVED]: Even granting an exact SVP oracle (beta -> infinity), beating det(L_W)^{1/(m+1)} requires (1/2 - sigma) > 1/(m + 1), i.e., (m + 1) * delta > log_2 N = 2 log_2 p total bits of bias about p across the m samples (with BKZ-beta, m * delta ~ log_2 N). Thus the generator problem literally asks to extract > log_2 N cumulative bits of approximate-multiple hints about p, amortized into delta = (log_2 N)^gamma bits per sample rather than Coppersmith's single (1/4) log_2 N block.
- Natural N-only biased families: None known. Pure trees have zero non-split bias (Theorem PT); depth-1 N-gates equidistribute off small-order events (leakmap_results.md:33-40, NE1); integer remainders N mod c_i concentrate mod c_i, not mod p, unless c_i already approximates p (classE_results.md:47); and our Round-1 toy falsified depth-2 PRIM, floor-squares, and Lucas V_N. Downgrade P(a < 1/3) from 0.4% to <= 0.1%.

Y4. G#2 (Kani 2^e-gluing over F_{l^2}):
- Verdict [PROVED kill of the Kani wrapper]: Yes — without auxiliary torsion images, Kani adds nothing and actually worsens algebraic degree. Over Z, mN = u^2 - u v + v^2 in the ~ (1/2) log_2 N bits of u, v (with carry bits) is already a quadratic Boolean system in O(log N) variables. Encoding nu' = u + v omega into an e-step Richelot chain over F_{l^2} replaces that degree-2 carry circuit by a composition of e ~ log_2 N rational maps of degree >= 2^e ~ N, with our Round-1 toy confirming zero local 2-adic prefix signal below k ~ 0.68 e (2^{2k} >= mN).
- Any free auxiliary torsion from N? [PROVED: O(1) bits only]: Norm nu_+ conj(nu_+) = N only cuts (Z[omega]/2^e)^2 to T_e (~ N candidates); rational torsion E_0(Q)_tors = Z/6Z fixes nu_+- mod 3 (O(1) bits, tracedata_results.md:214); and (x, y) -> (x^N, y^N) mod p equals (x(pi_p(P))^q, y(pi_p(P))^q), which leaves E_0 because z -> z^q is not a field morphism in char p. G#2 is killed (P < 0.05%).

Y5. G#3 (Joux-tower LP_exc^rel at unit rank >= 2) and C#3 (anomalous components):
- G#3: Observing that Theorem KH's envelope corollary requires e >= 3 (unit rank >= 2) to obtain a continuum S^{e-2} of incomparable unit cones is valid, but our Round-1 12-cone Minkowski LLL test on Q(zeta_7)^+ (e = 3, n = 4, m = 3) yielded 0 full-support vectors <= N^2 (min log|N_1 N_2|/log N = 3.345). Subsumed into subthird's existing 0.2% LP_exc^rel remainder.
- C#3: Dead (< 0.05%). CM discriminants D <= L_N[a] cover N^{-1/4+o(1)} of primes (nonsmooth_results.md:239), random curves hit a_p = 1 at N^{-1/4}, and genus g >= 2 Jacobians drop to Theta(1/p) = N^{-1/2}.

Y6. C's structural claim (unital maps Z/N -> char l need l | N):
- Ring maps [PROVED, airtight — even non-unital]: For ANY ring map phi: Z/N -> A into ANY F_l-algebra A (unital or not) with gcd(N, l) = 1, E = phi(1) satisfies N * E = phi(N) = 0 and l * E = 0, so Bezout u N + v l = 1 gives E = 0 and phi = 0 identically.
- Sweeping conclusion [FALSE as a proof, TRUE in outcome]: Non-ring transfers into char l != p, q DO exist, and each fails at a distinct quantitative barrier rather than unitality:
  1. Level-N moduli schemes in char 2: #X_1(N)(F_2) = phi(N)/2 and #X_0(N)(F_4) deterministically factor N over char 2 (geometry_results.md:66-73); blocked by genus/model size Theta(N).
  2. Group embeddings (Z/N)^x -> F_{2^k}^x: need lambda(N) | 2^k - 1, blocked by exponential degree k = ord_{lambda(N)}(2) ~ N and hidden order.
  3. Positional lifts (ADD_n -> F_2[T]) and global CM endomorphisms (G#2 over F_{l^2}): blocked by binary carries (T - 2)C(T) and missing 2^e-torsion hints.
  4. Weil restriction over Z/N stays in char p x q, hitting the poly(p) = N^{1/2} factor-base floor.

Y7. Joint verdict:
Treating factoring- and DL-equivalent primitives as targets was valuable diagnostically — exposing exact conservation laws (poly(p) factor bases, max(1 - beta, beta/2) >= 1/3, disc(Q_tilde) = -4kN, and (m + 1) delta > log_2 N) that block every known easy regime — but it is NOT a productive algorithmic direction for sub-L_N[1/3]. Every surviving candidate across both C and G collapses either to hidden-hint generation carrying > log_2 N total bits about p or to the two bare counting/decoding walls already isolated in subthird (beyond-Johnson 2D CRT list-decoding M2 and multi-cone unit cancellation LP_exc^rel). Within easy-regime transfers, no follow-up is warranted; across the whole project, at most one cheap falsification check remains worthwhile: testing multiplicative S-unit product steering (beyond linear Minkowski LLL) for LP_exc^rel at (e, n, m) = (3, 4, 3) over Q(zeta_7)^+, costing ~2 hours of Python with P(a < 1/3) ~ 0.2%. Overall combined probability of sub-L_N[1/3] via equivalent-target transfers is < 0.3%.
